\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For the symmetric three-state broadcast channel with admissible $-$1/2$\leq$lambda$\leq$1, is reconstruction on every b-ary tree $b\geq 2$ and observed Poisson(d) offspring tree $d>1$ equivalent to d $\lambda ^2>1$, including antiferromagnetic parameters and nonreconstruction at equality?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For the symmetric three-state broadcast channel with admissible $-$1/2$\leq$lambda$\leq$1, is reconstruction on every b-ary tree $b\geq 2$ and observed Poisson(d) offspring tree $d>1$ equivalent to d $\lambda ^2>1$, including antiferromagnetic parameters and nonreconstruction at equality?

